---
import Layout from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="Privacy policy for Ryan's Snowball (ryansnowball.com)."
	pubDate={new Date('September 07 2026')}
	lang="en"
	hasTranslation={true}
>
	<p>Last updated: 2026-09-07</p>

	<p>
		This page explains how <strong>Ryan's Snowball</strong> (ryansnowball.com, "this blog")
		handles visitor information.
	</p>

	<h2>What we collect</h2>
	<p>You can read this blog without creating an account or entering any personal information. Only a limited amount of data is handled:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>View counts</strong>: per-post view counts are tallied anonymously (Upstash Redis).
			No personally identifiable information is stored.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Hosting logs</strong>: this blog is hosted on Vercel, which may technically collect
			standard web server logs (IP address, request time, user agent, etc.). See the{' '}
			<a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>Vercel Privacy Policy</a
			> for details.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Comments (Giscus)</h2>
	<p>
		Post comments are powered by <strong>Giscus</strong>, built on GitHub Discussions. Leaving a
		comment requires signing in with a GitHub account, and comments are posted publicly to GitHub
		Discussions. GitHub's data handling is governed by the{' '}
		<a
			href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
			target="_blank"
			rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Privacy Statement</a
		>.
	</p>

	<h2>Advertising (Google AdSense)</h2>
	<p>This blog <strong>does not currently show ads.</strong> If Google AdSense is enabled in the future:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			Google and other third-party vendors may use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior
			visits to this or other websites.
		</li>
		<li>
			See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>Google's advertising policies</a
			> for how Google uses advertising cookies.
		</li>
		<li>
			Users can opt out of personalized advertising via{' '}
			<a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>Google Ads Settings</a
			>.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>This section will be updated once ads actually go live.</p>

	<h2>Cookies</h2>
	<p>
		Beyond what's strictly necessary to run the site, this blog does not currently use tracking
		cookies of its own. As noted above, using comments (Giscus) or, in the future, ads (Google
		AdSense) may cause those third parties to set their own cookies.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Questions about this policy? Please open an issue on{' '}
		<a
			href="https://github.com/Juhyeok-Ryan/ryans-automation-log/issues"
			target="_blank"
			rel="noopener noreferrer">this blog's GitHub repository</a
		>.
	</p>

	<h2>Changes</h2>
	<p>
		This policy may be updated as the blog evolves (e.g. if ads are introduced), and the "Last
		updated" date on this page will reflect that.
	</p>
</Layout>
